      "body": "# [Bugfix] Honor tokenizer_revision when building DeepSeek V4.1 Engram hashes\n\n## Purpose\n\n`NgramHashState` independently loads a tokenizer to build its compressed token\nmap. It currently passes `model_config.revision`, while the serving tokenizer\nuses `model_config.tokenizer_revision`. Explicitly selecting a tokenizer\nrevision can therefore load a different vocabulary for Engram, or fail if the\nmodel revision does not exist in the tokenizer repository.\n\nUse `tokenizer_revision` consistently. The existing ModelConfig fallback already\nhandles configurations that do not specify an independent tokenizer revision.\nNo hashing math, kernels, checkpoint weights, or serving parameters are changed.\n\nThe regression covers differing revisions, a tokenizer-only revision, and the\nsame-revision control. Two vocabularies have the same compressed vocabulary size\nbut different mappings; the test checks the actual constructed mapping rather\nthan only asserting a mocked call.\n\n## Duplicate Work\n\nOn 2026-09-21, searches for open PRs matching `Engram tokenizer` and issues\nmatching `\"Engram\" \"revision\"` found no fix for this selection mismatch. Other\nEngram kernel/performance/parallelism PRs address different behavior.\n\n## Test Result\n\nBase: `3c84ad13ed3f9fcd816bf1d15acb83c28cfa02f9`.\n\n- Focused regression on unchanged main: 2 failures, 1 passing same-revision control.\n- Local fixed source, real CPU torch/tokenizers/transformers: 3 passed.\n- Both modified files pass applicable pre-commit hooks.\n- H20 installed-code suite: 74 passed, 38 deselected (28 regression cases plus\n  46 existing CUDA/Triton cases, including graph replay). One unregistered\n  `distributed` marker warning comes from the isolated test configuration.\n- Restarted the real Flash TP8 H20 service with only these two source hunks\n  installed: 10/10 identical HTTP smoke cases pass before and after the change,\n  plus 5/5 additional unbiased image/color/counting checks after restart.\n  Runtime: vLLM `0.29.1rc1.dev422+gd05da62e9`, torch `2.13.0+cu130`,\n  real DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash weights, TP8+EP and DSpark (5 draft tokens,\n  adaptive verification disabled). The original versions of the two target\n  modules are byte-for-byte identical to the main base noted above.\n\nThe local CPU harness AST-loads source definitions and replaces unused vLLM\ntypes. It is not a full vLLM integration run. The GPU validation separately uses\nthe real installed vLLM runtime.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nFocused upstream regression command:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/kernels/test_engram.py -k uses_tokenizer_revision -q\n```\n\nThe H20 harness invoked pytest on the real installed modules with these arguments\n(the second file was staged from the separate vision-profiling fix):\n\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=7 PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 \\\n  .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q --tb=short --confcutdir=tests \\\n  -o addopts= -p no:cacheprovider \\\n  -k 'uses_tokenizer_revision or profile_image or default_profile or hash_cache_replay or lookback_window_reproduces or lookup_matches_torch or fused_engram_post_wkv' \\\n  tests/kernels/test_engram.py tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_deepseek_v41.py\n```\n\nBoth fixes were installed for the real-service integration run; only Engram's\nrevision selection and its regression belong to this PR. All requests were\nserial, capped at 128 output tokens. The smoke checks are not a comprehensive\nmodel accuracy benchmark, and no performance improvement is claimed.\n\n## Scope and Accountability\n\nThe change was developed with AI assistance (OpenAI Codex). The submitting human\nhas reviewed the changes and confirmed personally rerunning the relevant tests\nfor these new fixes successfully. Automated test results above were also\ncollected by the assistant; the submitter's confirmation is separate.\n\nA local-checkpoint service smoke test does not demonstrate independent remote\nrevision selection: a local tokenizer directory ignores Hub revision lookup.\nThe targeted revision regression provides that selection coverage. No claim is\nmade that this bug explains any prior production deadlock or corrupted output.\n",
